---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Q1 = `local function double(n)
    local answer = n * 2
end

local result = double(4)

print(result)`;

const Q2 = `local count = 10

local function reset(count)
    count = 0
    return count
end

reset(count)

print(count)`;

const Q4 = `PROCEDURE tally(scores, limit)
{
  n ← 0
  i ← 1
  REPEAT LENGTH(scores) TIMES
  {
    IF(scores[i] > limit)
    {
      n ← n + 1
    }
    i ← i + 1
  }
  RETURN(n)
}`;

const Q6 = `local function total(t)
    local sum = 0

    for i, v in ipairs(t) do
        sum = sum + v
        return sum
    end
end

print(total({4, 6, 10}))`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Question Set 5</h1>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">
          Six questions &middot; 10 minutes &middot; cumulative through 1.23
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            The last set before the exam. Six questions weighted toward{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">procedures</b>, and the whole quarter is
            fair game.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b>Set a timer for 10 minutes.</b> On paper, no computer.{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Mark each answer sure or unsure and then
            revise whatever the unsure ones point at</b> &mdash; that is what
            this set is for.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="questions">
          <h2>The Questions</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 1</h3>

          <p>What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Q1} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>8</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>nil</code></li>
            <li>(D) An error, because the function returns nothing</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 2</h3>

          <p>What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Q2} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>0</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>10</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>nil</code></li>
            <li>(D) An error, because <code>count</code> is used twice</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 3</h3>

          <p>
            In exam notation, a procedure hands a value back with:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>return expression</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>RETURN(expression)</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>DISPLAY(expression)</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>result &larr; expression</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 4</h3>

          <p>
            <code>tally([4, 12, 30, 8, 11], 10)</code> returns:
          </p>

          <Code code={Q4} frame="code" lang="txt" title="Exam notation" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>2</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>3</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>5</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>53</code></li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 5 &mdash; select all that apply</h3>

          <p>
            The Create Performance Task requires at least one{" "}
            <b>student-developed procedure</b>. Which of these would count?
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>love.draw</code>, with forty lines you wrote inside it</li>
            <li>(B) <code>love.keypressed(key)</code>, because it has a parameter</li>
            <li>(C) <code>drawShip(x, y, size)</code>, which you wrote and call twice</li>
            <li>(D) <code>tally(scores, limit)</code>, which you wrote and call once</li>
          </ul>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Question 6</h3>

          <p>What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Q6} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} class="mb-3" />

          <ul>
            <li>(A) <code>20</code></li>
            <li>(B) <code>4</code></li>
            <li>(C) <code>nil</code></li>
            <li>(D) <code>10</code></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Six answers with <b>sure</b> or <b>unsure</b> beside each, and your
            time. For question 5, list every letter you chose.
          </p>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">This is the last set before the exam.</b>{" "}
            Whatever you marked unsure is your revision list, and the four
            section summaries are where to look.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>4 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Start the Timer
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
